cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the MathTEC-Bench benchmark, please cite the dataset/code repository (this entry) and the paper below."
title: "MathTEC: A Multi-Agent Framework for Mathematical Text Error Correction"
abstract: >-
  MathTEC is a three-stage pipeline for correcting errors in mathematical text that mixes prose with inline LaTeX. It combines six-prompt ensemble detection, multi-agent debate, and optional post-check gates (a diff auditor and a LaTeX render check). The repository also releases MathTEC-Bench, a synthetic benchmark of 500 English mathematical statements spanning five error types.
